abstract={The proceedings contain 34 papers. The topics discussed include: a literature study to characterize continuous experimentation in software engineering; a metrics-based approach for assessing architecture-implementation mappings; a survey on the differences of using user story and tasks in the ASD effort estimation in Brazil; advances in a DSL to specify smart contracts for application integration processes; an experiment on how graduating students represent software designs; an overview of software architecture education; automatic identification of web API change types in consumer applications; autonomy and turnover in distributed software development projects: a systematic literature review; extending the sustainability-quality model for supporting the design of persuasive software systems; investigating the perception of success in software projects among developers from a Brazilian software company; and on the need to use smart contracts in enterprise application integration.},
