abstract={The proceedings contain 30 papers. The topics discussed include: using measurement and simulation for understanding distributed development processes in the cloud; identifying and mitigating risks of software project management in global software development; effective monitoring of progress of agile software development teams in modern software companies - an industrial case study; effort estimation for agile software development: comparative case studies using COSMIC functional size measurement and story points; autonomous real-time software & systems testing - a Six Sigma approach; using FSM patterns to size security non- functional requirements with cosmic; filling the gaps: imputation of missing metrics' values in quality models; discovering maintainability changes in large software systems; sustainable measurement programs for software development companies - what to measure; improving the real-time experience for software-measurement system end-users; automatically measuring the maintainability of service- and microservice-based systems - a literature review; automated analyses of model-driven artifacts: obtaining insights into real-life application of MDE; a rapid measurement procedure for sizing software applications based on cosmic FSM method; towards an automated functional size measurement procedure: an industrial case study; earned scope management: a case of study of scope performance using use cases as scope in a real project; and using weekly open defect reports as an indicator for software process efficiency -- theoretical framework and a longitudinal automotive industrial case study.},
