abstract={Among the various model-to-text transformation paradigms, template-based code generation (TBCG) is the most popular in MDE. Given the diversity of tools and approaches, it is necessary to classify and compare existing TBCG techniques to provide appropriate support to developers. We conduct a systematic mapping study of the literature to better understand the trends and characteristics of TBCG techniques over the past 16 years. We also evaluate the expressiveness, performance and scalability of the associated tools based on a range of models that implement critical patterns.},
