url={https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85010678663&doi=10.1007%2f978-3-319-51963-0_36&partnerID=40&md5=4d456feb0d2d90862d8996b08599d016},
abstract={Domain-specific languages (DSLs) assist a software developer (or end-user) in writing a program using idioms that are similar to the abstractions found in a specific problem domain. Indeed, the enhanced software productivity and reliability benefits that have been reported from DSL usage are hard to ignore and DSLs are flourishing. However, tool support for DSLs is lacking when compared to the capabilities provided for standard General-Purpose Languages (GPLs). For example, support for unit testing of a DSL program, as well as DSL debuggers, are rare. A Systematic Mapping Study (SMS) has been performed to better understand the DSL research field, identify research trends, and any possible open issues. In this talk I will first introduce DSLs by discussing when and how to develop DSLs, then results from SMS will be presented along with open DSL problems such as lacking tool support for DSLs and difficulties in combining DSLs. © Springer International Publishing AG 2017.},
references={Barišić, A., Amaral, V., Goulão, M., Barroca, B., Evaluating the usability of domain-specific languages (2013) Chapter 14, Formal, pp. 386-407. , Mernik, M. (ed.), Practical Aspects of Domain-Specific Languages: Recent Developments; Barrett, E., Bolz, C.F., Tratt, L., Approaches to interpreter composition (2015) Comput. Lang. Syst. Struct, 44C, pp. 199-217; Bravenboer, M., Kalleberg, K.T., Vermaas, R., Visser, E., Stratego/XT 0.17. A language and toolset for program transformation (2008) Sci. Comput. Program, 72 (1-2), pp. 52-70; Carver, J.C., Syriani, E., Gray, J., Assessing the frequency of empirical evaluation in software modeling research (2011) Proceedings of the First Workshop on Experiences and Empirical Studies in Software Modelling, Paper 5; Chis, A., Denker, M., Gîrba, T., Nierstrasz, O., Practical domain-specific debuggers using the moldable debugger framework (2015) Comput. Lang. Syst. Struct, 44A, pp. 89-113; Čeh, I., Črepinšek, M., Kosar, T., Mernik, M., Ontology driven development of domain-specific languages (2011) Comput. Sci. Inf. Syst, 8 (2), pp. 317-342; Efftinge, S., Völter, M., OAW xText: A framework for textual DSLs (2006) Workshop on Modeling Symposium at Eclipse Summit; Erdweg, S., Giarrusso, P.G., Rendel, T., Language composition untangled (2012) Proceedings of Workshop on Language Descriptions, Tools and Applications (LDTA 2012); Erdweg, S., Van Der Storm, T., Völter, M., Tratt, L., Bosman, R., Cook, W.R., Gerritsen, A., Van Der Woning, J., Evaluating and comparing language workbenches: Existing results and benchmarks for the future (2015) Comput. Lang. Syst. Struct, 44A, pp. 24-47; Fowler, M., (2010) Domain Specific Languages, , Addison-Wesley, Boston; Gabriel, P., Goulão, M., Amaral, V., Do software languages engineers evaluate their languages? (2010) XIII Congreso Iberoamericano En “Software Engineering” (Cibse 2010), pp. 149-162; Ghosh, D., DSL for the uninitiated (2011) Commun. ACM, 54 (7), pp. 44-50; Karakoidas, V., Mitro