volume={0},
pages={200-205},
doi={10.1109/CIST.2016.7805042},
art_number={7805042},
note={cited By 5; Conference of 4th IEEE International Colloquium on Information Science and Technology, CiSt 2016 ; Conference Date: 24 October 2016 Through 26 October 2016;  Conference Code:125733},
url={https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85010192583&doi=10.1109%2fCIST.2016.7805042&partnerID=40&md5=eae457bcfdf9d35ddb31f6ef57576d1e},
abstract={Automation and generation of complex solutions is a flowering field that is gaining ground day by day to this the need for a study to collect all the recent research development in this area. In fact, the research is very abundant in some point that research have not away or who are just redundant. The overall objective of this paper is to plot the landscape of published proposals in the field of automation and code generation, without restricting the search neither to a specific context nor to a particular programming language. We decide in our article to combine two interesting approaches which permit to focus effectively a given field: Tertiary review and Systematic mapping review; this combination is very constructive and allow us to enlarge and feed our study. Our review is based on a comprehensive set of 2450 selected resources over 6223 studies that were initially identified: 2347 secondary articles, and 103 primary articles selected. As a result of our study we conclude that there is need for research that validates and evaluates the existing proposals. © 2016 IEEE.},
references={Dom, E., Pérez, B., Rubio, Á.L., A systematic review of code generation proposals from state machine specifications (2012) Information and Software Technology, 54 (10), pp. 1045-1066; Mehmood, A., Jawawi, A.D.N., Aspect-oriented modeldriven code generation: A systematic mapping study (2013) Information and Software Technology, 55 (2), pp. 395-411; Tosi, D., Morasca, S., Supporting the semi-automatic semantic annotation of web services: A systematic literature review (2015) Information and Software Technology, 61, pp. 16-32; Gurunule, D., Nashipudimath, M., A review: Analysis of aspect orientation and model driven engineering for code generation (2015) Procedia Computer Science, 45, pp. 852-861; Ameller, D., Development of service-oriented architectures using model-driven development: A mapping study (2015) Information and Software Technology, 62, pp. 42-66; González, C.A., Cabot, J., Formal verification of static software models in MDE: A systematic review (2014) Information and Software Technology, 56 (8), pp. 821-838; Mehmood, A., Jawawi, A.D.N., A comparative survey of aspect-oriented code generation approaches (2011) Software Engineering (MySEC), 2011 5th Malaysian Conference In., , IEEE; Nguyen, P.H., An extensive systematic review on the Model-Driven Development of secure systems (2015) Information and Software Technology, 68, pp. 62-81; Nascimento, D., Marques, L., A systematic mapping study on domain specific languages (2012) Proc. 7th Int. Conf. Softw. Eng. Advances (ICSEA'12); Nascimento, L.M., Domain-specific languages-a systematic mapping study (2012) Proceeedings of 7th International Conference on Software Engineering Advances (ICSEA).; Batouta, Z.I., Dehbi, R., Talea, M., Hajoui, O., Multi-criteria analysis and advanced comparative study between automatic generation approaches in software engineering (2015) Journal of Theoretical and Applied Information Technology, 81 (3); Lütjen, M., Model-driven logistics engineering-challenges of model a