pages={122-127},
note={cited By 2},
url={https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84941118971&partnerID=40&md5=3a7f3da58709444d75fff28700fad471},
abstract={Among different Model Driven Engineering (MDE) approaches, the Object Management Group (OMG) adopted the Model Driven Architecture (MDA). The MDA approach is aiming to automate the software develop process by using models instead of conventional coding and bases on the separation of concern concept. In June 2014, the OMG released the second version of the MDA guide trying to realize the fundamental principles and to support the first MDA guide issued in 2003 with more detailed specifications. A gap of 11 years makes researchers from their own perspective and background come up with different interpretations of the MDA terms. The thing that generates a confusion of what is beyond and what is within the MDA scope. By strictly referring to the MDA standard (not to model-driven engineering in general), we provide in this work a review of the current MDA literature. We also shed the light on the MDA research directions, specifically on the automations of the MDA development process and its targeted platforms. © 2005 - 2015 JATIT & LLS. All rights reserved.},
references={Corba, O., (1998), IIOP2.3specification, 1998; Siegel, J., OMG Overview: CORBA and the OMA in Enterprise Computing (1998) Communications of the ACM, 41 (10), pp. 37-43; Soley, R.M., Andreas, W., (1995) Object Management Architecture Guide: Revision 2.0, , Wiley; (2001) O.D., OMG: Unified Modeling Language V1.4, , formal/01-09-67, OMG Document: formal/01-09-67, Sept.2001; OMG: Meta Object Facility (MOF) v1.3.1 (2001) OMG Document: Formal; Omg, X., (2000) Metadata Interchange (XMI) Specification, , http://www.omg.org/docs/formal/05-05-01.pdf, (accessed October 10, 2005); Chang, D.T., Common Warehouse Metamodel (CWM), UML and XML (2000) Meta Data Conference, , (March 19-23, 2000); Poole, J.D., Model-driven architecture: Vision, standards and emerging technologies (2001) Workshop on Metamodeling and Adaptive Object Models, ECOOP; MDA Guide Version1.0.1. 2003, , Version 1.0.1; (2014), MDA Guide revision 2.0; Soares, I.W., Modeling of embedded software on MDA platform models (2012) Journal of Computer Science & Technology, 12p; Almeida, J.P., (2004) On the Notion of Abstract Platform in MDA Development. In Enterprise Distributed Object Computing Conference, EDOC 2004, , Proceedings. Eighth IEEE International, IEEE; Mellor, S.J., (2004) MDA Distilled: Principles of Model-Driven Architecture, , Addison-Wesley Professional; Dobing, B., Parsons, J., Dimensions of UML diagram use: A survey of practitioners (2008) Journal of Database Management (JDM), 19 (1), pp. 1-18; Czarnecki, K., Helsen, S., Classification of model transformation approaches (2003) Proceedings of the 2Nd OOPSLA Workshop on Generative Techniques in the Context of the Model Driven Architecture; Soley, R., Model driven architecture (2000) OMG White Paper, 308, 308p; Gerber, A., Transformation: The missing link of MDA (2002) Graph Transformation, pp. 90-105. , Springer; Oldevik, J., Toward standardised model to text transformations Model Driven Architecture-Foundations and Applications, , Springer; W