abstract={The proceedings contain 36 papers. The topics discussed include: systematic literature reviews in global software development: a tertiary study; preliminary results of a systematic review on requirements evolution; causes of requirement change - a systematic literature review; a systematic mapping study on the open source software development process; a study on risk management for software engineering; an initial evaluation of requirements dependency types in change propagation analysis; a mapping study of the definitions for service oriented architecture; towards an explanatory theory of motivation in software engineering: a qualitative case study of a government organization; maturity of software modelling and model driven engineering: a survey in the Italian industry; evaluation of traceability recovery in context: a taxonomy for information retrieval tools; and the influence of human aspects on software process improvement: qualitative research findings and comparison to previous studies.},
