abstract={Manufacturers of the medical device market in Europe should be prepared for some upcoming changes as 2007 amendment to the Medical Devices Directive (MDD) 93/42/EEC will come into force in March 2010. A CE report is a literature review that is submitted to the notified body to augment or substitute for new clinical data. The findings applied to Class I and Class II a devices, as well as Class II b and Class III devices. The Clinical Evaluation Task Force, a subgroup of the MDEG, proposed the changes found in Directive 2007/47/EC that led to the amendments of MDD 93/42/EEC. The clinical investigation plan shall contain a critical review of the relevant scientific literature and/or unpublished data and reports together with a list of the literature reviewed. It must be remembered that the ISO 14155 standards are adopted by the Committee for European Normalization and incorporated by reference into the directives.},
